                <pb facs="0856" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Trueblood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-02T12:00:00-04:32">July 2, 1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        1:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. The Minister for Foreign Affairs informed me this morning at 12 that the
                    situation was unchanged, with Bolivia still waiting for the Paraguayan reply.
                    Other officials of the Foreign Office stated as their motive that the Bolivian
                    Minister at Asuncion would have to leave. The Paraguayan Minister has had no
                    advices from his Government.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">La Razon</hi> this morning praised Bolivia’s acceptance
                    in principle of the Argentine proposal which it stated depended on the
                    Paraguayan answer. The Argentine Minister conferred again this morning with the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <p>The Brazilian Chargé d’Affaires is visiting the Minister for Foreign Affairs this
                    afternoon to express his Government’s hope that a break can be avoided. He
                    feels, however, that it is now up to Paraguay since Bolivia has shown its desire
                    to settle the matter amiably by its second note as well as by not retiring its
                    Minister earlier.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trueblood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
